 runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids the November to December pair came in under 90% of normal in 36 of 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 35% of normal in January to February and 163% in July to August. For 2026 so far, February to March sat at 24% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 25332 had its driest year in 1956 at 54%.</p>"}
